# HEM-6232T (Z identity): first-time pairing (key registration). Omron registers user 2 on this two-user model; OpenPressure programs the shared key and reads both banks on the same connection.
# Omron selects HEM-6232T-Z from the advertised IDs (category 0x0000, model 0x0144); OpenPressure maps the
# Device Information model HEM-6232T (also Omron's config model_id) to its two-bank 14-byte map.
name hem-6232t/pair
flow pair
register user=2
advertise name=BLEsmart_000001440011223344 services=ecbe3980-c9a2-11e1-b1bd-0002a5d5c51b
# Synthetic Device Information; Omron reads the revisions and the System ID during connection setup.
dis model=HEM-6232T firmware=0001 software=0001 systemid=0011223344556677
time 2026-01-02T03:04:05 zone=UTC
key 05050505050505050505050505050505

alias unlock b305b680-aee7-11e1-a730-0002a5d5c51b
alias tx db5b55e0-aee7-11e1-965e-0002a5d5c51b,e0b8a060-aee7-11e1-92f4-0002a5d5c51b,0ae12b00-aee8-11e1-a192-0002a5d5c51b,10e1ba60-aee8-11e1-89e5-0002a5d5c51b
alias rx 49123040-aee8-11e1-a74d-0002a5d5c51b,4d0bf320-aee8-11e1-a0d9-0002a5d5c51b,5128ce60-aee8-11e1-b84b-0002a5d5c51b,560f1420-aee8-11e1-8184-0002a5d5c51b
alias clock 00002a2b-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb

# 14-byte records with adjacent byte pairs swapped, sequence number 1, Omron record checksum in both bytes
# of the last pair: user 1 130/78 mmHg, pulse 67, 2025-07-09 06:14:38; user 2 120/80, pulse 70, 2025-08-01 07:30:00.
memory fill=ff
memory 0x2e8 4e691943 1d2603a6 0000 0001 0000
memory 0x860 505f1946 20270780 0000 0001 dddd
# Index (index_setting_read_address=260), byte pairs swapped: per user next write position 1, one unsent
# record, sequence number 1.
memory 0x260 0001 0001 0001 0001 00010000 00010000

# Enter key mode, program the key.
write unlock 02 00000000000000000000000000000000
notify unlock 8200
write unlock 00 05050505050505050505050505050505
notify unlock 8000
# OpenPressure follows the pinned omblepy order and unlocks with the new key.
[ours-only: Omron does not follow registration with 01 (docs/protocol.md, observed in the sandbox)] write unlock 01 05050505050505050505050505050505
[ours-only: acknowledgment for the unlock above] notify unlock 8100

write tx 08 00 00 00 00 10 00 18
notify rx 18 80 00 00 00 10 00 01 02 03 04 05 06 07 08 09 0a 0b 0c 0d 0e 0f 00 88

[omron-only: Omron reads the index block (index_setting_read_address 0x260) before records] reads 0x260 44 chunk=44
[omron-only: Omron reads setting-info block 3 (index_setting_info_read_address 0x270 + 28)] reads 0x28c 16 chunk=16

[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings (hem-7156t/pair, hem-7155t/pair)] reads 0x2e8 1400 chunk=16
[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings (hem-7156t/pair, hem-7155t/pair)] reads 0x860 1400 chunk=16

[ours-only: OpenPressure clock sync via Current Time; Omron writes setting block 3 instead (docs/omron-sandbox.md)] write clock ea 07 01 02 03 04 05 05 00 01

# Omron Connect 2026.09.03 post-pairing settings frames from this synthetic fixture.
[omron-only: Omron Connect 2026.09.03 Pair user 2, index prefix with the registered user's cleared unsent counter at 0x2a4; docs/omron-sandbox.md] write tx 1801c002a410 00010001000180000001000000010000 00ee
[omron-only: synthetic full echo acknowledgment; the physical monitor reply is unconfirmed] notify rx 1881c002a410 00010001000180000001000000010000 006e
[omron-only: Omron Connect 2026.09.03 Pair user 2, clock block 3 (fixture time + 1 s) merged with birthday block 2 at 0x2c2; docs/omron-sandbox.md] write tx 2601c002c21e 0100ff01fffffffffffffffffff9ffffffffffffffff011a03020604ff22 0005
[omron-only: synthetic full echo acknowledgment; the physical monitor reply is unconfirmed] notify rx 2681c002c21e 0100ff01fffffffffffffffffff9ffffffffffffffff011a03020604ff22 0085

write tx 08 0f 00 00 00 00 00 07
notify rx 08 8f 00 00 00 00 00 87

[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings (hem-7156t/pair, hem-7155t/pair)] expect reading user=1 sys=130 dia=78 pulse=67 time=2025-07-09T06:14:38
[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings (hem-7156t/pair, hem-7155t/pair)] expect reading user=2 sys=120 dia=80 pulse=70 time=2025-08-01T07:30:00
